  "id": "cold-cognition",
  "term": "cold cognition",
  "definition": "Cold cognition refers to thinking processes that are relatively independent of emotion, in contrast to hot cognition, which is emotion-laden. In this context, it describes cognitive processing that is not driven by emotional content.",
